---
title: Lift Up Your Heads, Ye Mighty Gates
type: hymn
hymn_number: 436
tune: Truro
words: Georg Weissel (1590-1635); tr. Catherine Winkworth (1827-1878)
music: Truro, melody from Psalmodia Evangelica, Part II, 1789
---

<!-- One verse per slide. [1], [2] … are verse numbers (shown on the stream). -->
[1] Lift up your heads, ye mighty gates;
behold, the King of glory waits!
The King of kings is drawing near;
the Savior of the world is here.

---

[2] O blest the land, the city blest,
where Christ the ruler is confessed!
O happy hearts and happy homes
to whom this King of triumph comes!

---

[5] So come, my Sovereign; enter in!
Let new and nobler life begin;
thy Holy Spirit guide us on,
until the glorious crown be won.
